00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:46,437
which will result in the maximum penalty.

263
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,380
Sounds good.

264
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,109
I like that better anyway.

265
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:52,777
Giving a hand to that Roger guy
is something I'll never forget.

266
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:56,220
In fact, it's something
I take great pride in.

267
00:16:58,500 --> 00:16:59,840
He's proud of that?

268
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:03,837
I can't believe he'd make such a bold
claim about something so despicable.

269
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:04,750
Traitor!

270
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:05,930
Fishman!

271
00:17:06,013 --> 00:17:07,900
You regret that! Why, Tom?

272
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,300
Tell me!

273
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:10,900
It's for the best.

274
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:12,640
Now, listen.

275
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,760
Don't blame yourself for this.

276
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:17,397
I never thought the world government would

277
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:19,951
go to such extremes to get the blueprints.

278
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:23,720
And the situation with Roger
only makes the matter worse.

279
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,017
Even so, it doesn't have to be this way!

280
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:27,120
No, it's fine.

281
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,380
Look around you.

282
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:31,900
Even if I'm charged with
a crime from 14 years ago,

283
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:36,037
nothing else about this town is
the same now as it was back then.

284
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,080
This island is alive and strong.

285
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:40,128
This is only the beginning.

286
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,720
No matter what ends up happening to me,

287
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:46,220
I was still able to help this town.

288
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:53,320
My dream has finally begun to run.

289
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,620
Tom, don't please!

290
00:17:58,900 --> 00:17:59,960
Tom, no!

291
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:10,260
Iceberg, Franky, take
care of the blueprints.

292
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:16,900
Kokoro, Yokozuna, thank
you for everything.

293
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:24,060
The tranquilizers finally kicked in!

294
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,477
Capture those three for
the judicial ship attack!

295
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:27,390
Yes, sir!

296
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,550
Hold it.

297
00:18:29,633 --> 00:18:36,377
I'm amending the charges for the crime of
designing and building a ship for gold.

298
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,290
Roger.

299
00:18:37,373 --> 00:18:38,203
The king of the pirates.

300
00:18:38,286 --> 00:18:41,877
Tom and Tom alone will be apprehended
and taken to Annie's Lobby.

301
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:43,377
That is all.

302
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:49,437
What in the hell got into
that old geezer's head?

303
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:50,350
Whatever.

304
00:18:50,433 --> 00:18:52,337
I don't need his lackeys.

305
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:54,260
Release those two. apprentices.

306
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,680
Tom can't be saved from this.

307
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:06,077
It's the government we're up against.

308
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:08,800
There's nothing we can do. Endure it.

309
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:11,380
Tom traded his life for yours.

310
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:15,957
If you make them your enemy, you won't be
able to win, no matter how many lives you?

311
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:16,870
have to give.

312
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:20,777
Annie's lobby is the government's
personal judicial island.

313
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:25,437
Not one single person who's been
sent to that dreadful place has ever

314
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:30,837
been seen again the C train is
ready for departure sir we can leave

315
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:35,817
anytime you like very good let's

316
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:38,257
get moving men load up the prisoner

317
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:43,940
I can't this bloated fish man is
He's going for a little train ride.

318
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:45,940
Endure this!

319
00:19:56,460 --> 00:19:57,620
Stop it!

320
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:07,000
Really messed up his face.

321
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:09,980
Trump's apprentice is
the one on a rampage.

322
00:20:10,260 --> 00:20:11,117
No, stop!

323
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,141
Let her get him!

324
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:13,517
Capture that criminal!

325
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,894
The rest of you, take Tom to the train!

326
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:17,620
That's not gonna happen!

327
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:19,806
Nobody's taking him anywhere!

328
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:21,020
Fire at will!

329
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,460
I'm staying right here!

330
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:28,720
Are you okay?

331
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:29,900
After him!

332
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:32,110
Hurry!

333
00:20:32,193 --> 00:20:33,023
Get out of here!

334
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:33,936
Fire!

335
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:46,080
Damn it!

336
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:47,140
He got away!

337
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:51,292
I'll get that Cutty Flam brat
if it's the last thing I do!

338
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:53,777
That little criminal will
pay for what he's done!

339
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:58,154
Mark my words, once this case is over,
I'll have him sent to the gallows!

340
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,438
Spandam, he's here!

341
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:00,490
What?

342
00:21:00,573 --> 00:21:01,403
Now!

343
00:21:01,486 --> 00:21:02,316
It's...

344
00:21:02,399 --> 00:21:03,740
it's Cutty Flam, sir! What? Where?

345
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:05,957
Standing out on the tracks ahead of us,

346
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:09,158
and it appears that he's
holding some sort of weapon!

347
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,400
Stay right there, Yokozuna.

348
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:19,040
He's out of his mind!

349
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:20,653
What should we do, sir?

350
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:22,845
Are you out of your mind, too?

351
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:24,180
We keep on going.

352
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:26,217
That's what he wants us to do, right?

353
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:29,140
Don't worry about him. Right. Yes, sir.

354
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:34,111
All right, Puffing Top, that's far enough.

355
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:38,097
What do you think you're doing?

356
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:40,180
Where are you taking your creator?

357
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:56,540
I won't let you pass.

358
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:03,680
Give me Tom back!

359
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:07,280
You hear me?

360
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:09,100
Stop now, Katorea!

361
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,580
I see, so your parents
just abandoned you, huh?

362
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:17,780
That's terrible.

363
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:21,180
Hey, stop laughing at me! Fine, then.

364
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:22,640
Come stay with me.

365
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:26,720
Tom, I don't want to build ships anymore.

366
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:32,468
I can't love ships that hurt
the people I care so much about.

367
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:34,240
I won't do it.

368
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:40,300
And even so, my goal in
life is to be just like you.

369
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:51,360
Come back.

370
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:54,480
Come back and teach me once again.

371
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:07,400
Because someday, I want to
build my own dream ship.

372
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:16,217
A ship that will proudly
sail bravely over uncharted

373
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:19,860
waters all the way to
the ends of the world.
